<title>THAILAND: Premier sells stakes in subsidiaries.</title>
<headline>Premier sells stakes in subsidiaries.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1997-05-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Diversified Thai trading and manufacturing firm Premier Enterprise Plc will sell holdings in three subsidiaries, the company said in a statement on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The company said it would sell a 15 percent holding, or 750,000 shares, in trading firm Premier Marketing Co Ltd at 370 baht per share for 277.50 million baht ($11 million).</p>
<p>American International Assurance Co Ltd and AIG Asia Direct Investment Fund Ltd will each buy 375,000 shares, the firm said.</p>
